---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';

const SCHEDULING_LINK = "https://calendar.app.google/ZgCjgA8Mk3tosTmh9";
---

<MarketingLayout
	title="Work | People Purpose Product"
	description="Three ways I work as the product owner for funded mission-driven teams: a product studio, a fractional seat, and a coaching program."
>
	<section class="page-header">
		<h1>Work</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			Most funded mission-driven teams never had a product owner. I work as theirs,
			and I leave the team able to do the job without me. The work is judgment, not
			delivery: what to build, in what order, and how we know it worked.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="services">
		<article class="service">
			<h2>Product studio</h2>
			<p class="what">
				I own the roadmap and bring the engineers. You get a working product, and a
				team that understands why it was built this way.
			</p>
			<p class="fit"><b>Fits when</b> you have funding and a real problem, and nobody inside to run the build.</p>
		</article>

		<article class="service">
			<h2>Fractional product owner</h2>
			<p class="what">
				I take the product owner seat on your team. I draft the requirements, design
				the experiments, read the data, and make the call, with your people in the room.
			</p>
			<p class="fit"><b>Fits when</b> you already have engineers, and nobody deciding what they build.</p>
		</article>

		<article class="service">
			<h2>Product owner coaching</h2>
			<p class="what">
				A program that trains your people to do this job. We draft the roadmap together,
				run the experiments together, and watch ideas flop together, until your team can
				do it without me.
			</p>
			<p class="fit"><b>Fits when</b> someone on your team is already doing this job and never had anyone to learn it from.</p>
		</article>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>The studio and the fractional seat look alike from the outside</h2>
		<p>
			The difference is who owns the roadmap. In the studio I own it. In the fractional
			seat you own it, and I sit in it with you.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>How it goes</h2>
		<p>
			With you, not for you. We draft the roadmap together, put the product in real
			hands fast, and watch the ideas that do not work fail early enough to be cheap.
			Engineering makes sure the thing is built right. I make sure it is the right thing.
		</p>
		<p>
			Every engagement ends the same way: your team can do this without me.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section closing">
		<h2>Start a conversation</h2>
		<p>
			If any of this resonates, I'd love to talk. Book 30 minutes to go over what you
			are working on and where I can help.
		</p>
		<a href={SCHEDULING_LINK} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="cta-button">
			Find a time →
		</a>
		<p class="schedule-note">
			Prefer email? Write me at <a class="email-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicknorena/">hello at this domain</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</MarketingLayout>

<script>
	// Assemble the address in the browser so scrapers reading the raw HTML
	// never see a complete email. The href above is a fallback (LinkedIn)
	// for the rare no-JS visitor.
	const user = 'hello';
	const domain = 'peoplepurposeproduct.com';
	const address = `${user}@${domain}`;
	document.querySelectorAll('.email-link').forEach((el) => {
		el.setAttribute('href', `mailto:${address}`);
		el.textContent = address;
	});
</script>

<style>
	.page-header {
		padding: 3em 0 2.5em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		margin-bottom: 3em;
	}
	.page-header h1 {
		font-size: 3rem;
		line-height: 1.1;
	}
	.page-header .lede {
		margin-top: 1em;
		max-width: 720px;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.services {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2.5em;
		margin-bottom: 3em;
		padding-bottom: 3em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}
	.service {
		max-width: 720px;
	}
	.service h2 {
		font-size: 1.375rem;
		margin: 0 0 0.4em;
	}
	.service .what {
		margin: 0 0 0.6em;
	}
	.service .fit {
		margin: 0;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}

	.content-section {
		margin-bottom: 3em;
		padding-bottom: 3em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		max-width: 720px;
	}
	.content-section h2 {
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75em;
	}
	.closing {
		border-bottom: none;
	}

	.cta-button {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-top: 0.5em;
		padding: 0.75em 1.5em;
		background: var(--accent);
		color: white;
		text-decoration: none;
		border-radius: 8px;
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.cta-button:hover {
		background: var(--accent-dark);
		color: white;
	}
	.schedule-note {
		margin-top: 1.25em;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.page-header h1 {
			font-size: 2.25rem;
		}
	}
</style>
